{
  "name": "Planning Your New Shower: A Step-by-Step Guide",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Thinking about a new shower? Awesome! Let's break down what usually happens when you’re getting a new shower installed. First up is demo day. This is when the old shower, and sometimes even parts of the wall, come out. It can get a little dusty, but it's the exciting beginning! Next, the framing and prep work begins. This ensures everything is structurally sound for your new shower. Then comes the super important part: waterproofing. This step is critical for preventing leaks down the line, and it’s where a lot of DIY projects go wrong if not done precisely. After that, your shower pan or base gets installed, creating the floor of your new shower. Then, it's time for the wall surround or tile installation, where your design really starts to come to life. Once that's in, the fixtures like your showerhead and controls are hooked up. Finally, if you're getting a glass enclosure or door, that goes in, and everything gets sealed up. There’s usually a cure time for adhesives and sealants before you can actually use it, so patience is key! Getting a pro like HH Remodeling LLC involved can really smooth out these steps, especially for custom tile work or when plumbing needs to be adjusted.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
